  "body": "Work package: https://openproject.romaine.life/wp/APPS-57\n\nShows opened at an already-watched episode because several round entries could be `playing` at once, and startup took the earliest. Now a file load moves `playing` to its entry in one transaction (the one it leaves returns to `watched` or `pending` by its episode's watched status), a partial unique index allows one per playlist, and startup resumes at it. Opening a database without the index first demotes the extras, keeping the most recently updated episode's entry; on a copy of the live database that keeps Daredevil and returns the Daily Show episode to `watched`.\n\nContract: round-and-advance M3 is rewritten to this rule; Play Show's own reset is removed since the load now does it. Watched status is unchanged.",
